across the whole winning ancestry before changing code: every necessary ancestor checkpoint must be admitted, and checkpoint created_by_host_id must match its owning lease holder. Drive positive multi-generation control and missing/wrong ancestor checkpoint and wrong creator negatives through BuildPlan, old-plan Revalidate, AuthoritativeStatus and AuthoritativeList. Preserve valid branching, lagging copies, canonical identity, required parked-source refusal and all seven capability names. Do not reopen closed prior review findings or reduce the task/AC denominator. Add focused qualifying narrowing mutants for these missing semantic guards with actual applied passing survivor through the same instrument. Bind evidence to final source and correct the prior gofmt command exit-2 description (absent cmd directory); do not claim old failed evidence clean. Retain full local required validation. No hosted CI. Handoff an uncommitted complete candidate via normal task-board CR lifecycle for independent review; no manual integration or destructive Git commands.\n\n\n\n### TASK-260830-21gygk_reviewer-after-rev5.md\nReview the next immutable candidate after CR5 rework against the full assigned v0.6.0 selector/plan/summary scope. Read the CR5 verdict/evidence and producer outcome. Independently verify closure of TestRev5AncestorCheckpointAuthority and TestRev5CheckpointCreatorMustBeHolder using valid positive controls. Exercise BuildPlan, old-plan Revalidate and both authoritative summary entries. Validate every necessary ancestry checkpoint's session, lease and creator relationship, preserving valid branching and missing-versus-unavailable distinctions. A canonical digest alone is not semantic admission. Audit the relevant 5.3/5.4 relationships as a whole to catch the recurring missing-gate family rather than accepting only the two fixture fixes.\nRetain closed findings: canonical Lease Record identity, lagging copies, required parked sources, seven capabilities, live changed-record refusal and previously established predecessor/reducer/enum behavior. Do not repeat unrelated closed audits without new evidence. Shared API caller boundary is accepted; do not shrink remaining assigned requirements.\nCheck final-source provenance and actual exits for new narrowing mutants and same-instrument applied survivor; NOT_APPLIED/compile failure are not behavioral kills. Corrected formatting evidence must use existing paths. Reuse trustworthy exact-source prior evidence with explicit bounds; run necessary new independent regressions. All CI is local. Never edit the active product candidate or integrate; attach task-scoped verdict and raw evidence, then route accept_cr or changes requested through the normal lifecycle.\n\n\n\n### TASK-260830-21gygk_rework-rev6.md\nAttached file: `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-21gygk/TASK-260830-21gygk_rework-rev6.md`\n\n- Byte count: `2183`\n- Content digest: `sha256:f366940896a06c99b9d895b6cc9df27d63619f290c91fdc65471b7b79a4d0449`\n- Access: read-only\n\n\n\n\n\n## Evidence and Safety\n\n- Add/update a task-scoped outcome named `TASK-260830-21gygk_*` before handoff:\n  `task-board m 'add_resource(TASK-260830-21gygk, name=TASK-260830-21gygk_results.md, content=\"...\", type=outcome, description=\"Handoff evidence\")'`\n- Gating, refusing, validating, authorizing, or attesting behavior ships with negative tests that fail when the gate admits what it must reject; prove the bound by narrowing it, not only by deleting it, and name the production call site. Shapes and incidents: `references/negative-evidence.md`.\n- An absence and a failure to read are different facts; report unknown instead of inferring a property from a proxy signal.\n- Stop-The-Line only for an evidence-backed external blocker or unresolved human-only product/platform/architecture/approval decision. Persist evidence, failed attempts, options/tradeoffs, recommendation, and exact input needed; otherwise rework autonomously.\n- `to-review` is a role handoff, not accepted completion. Report **ready for review** or **handed off to review**.\n\n## LAST — Run For Role Handoff\n\nAfter AC, checklist, validation, and outcome evidence:\n\n```bash\ntask-board handoff TASK-260830-21gygk --role developer\n```\n\n## Working Directory\nBoard directory: `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.task-board`\n\nWork in the project root. Never edit board files directly.\n\n## Story Workspace\n\nYou are running in an isolated Git worktree for STORY-260830-3tq4ns.\n\n- Workspace path: `.temp/STORY-260830-3tq4ns/worktree` (this is your working directory)\n- Branch: `task-board/story/STORY-260830-3tq4ns`, forked from `main`\n- Authoritative board: `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.task-board` (already exported as `TASK_BOARD_DIR`)\n\nMake every repository change here. Do not commit, switch, rebase, merge, or delete this branch, and do not run `task-board` against the `.task-board` copy inside this worktree — it is a checkout artifact, not the board. Integration into trunk is the orchestrator's step, not yours.\n\nLeave your work UNCOMMITTED in the worktree — the handoff snapshots the working tree against the recorded checkpoint. A commit of your own on this branch is refused at handoff with `change_request_candidate_committed_past_checkpoint`, and the repair is `git reset --soft <checkpoint_oid>` before completing again.\n"}}
