7|  parses `created_by_host_id` as UUIDv7 (`invalid_config` when malformed).\n28|- `checkLeaseChain` now returns the winner-to-root ancestry chain in\n29|  addition to the direct predecessor (walk semantics unchanged).\n30|- `checkWinnerCheckpoint` additionally enforces checkpoint creator ==\n31|  owning lease holder (predecessor holder at epoch > 1, self at epoch 1).\n32|- New `checkAncestorCheckpoints` + `checkCheckpointBinding` validate\n33|  every non-winner lease of the winning ancestry: epoch > 1 must\n34|  reference an admitted checkpoint for its session and predecessor\n35|  lease with creator == predecessor holder; the epoch-1 root may omit\n36|  the reference, otherwise it must bind to itself with creator == its\n37|  holder. Unresolvable/misbound references refuse\n38|  `selector_observation_unavailable`. Only the winner's ancestry is\n39|  consulted, so legal branching, lagging copies, canonical identity,\n40|  and parked-source refusal are preserved.\n41|- `winningLeaseFor` (shared by BuildPlan/bindPlan, Revalidate,\n42|  authorize/AuthoritativeStatus/AuthoritativeList) runs all three\n43|  checks, so old-plan invalidation after loss of ancestor checkpoint\n44|  falls out of the same gate.\n45|\n46|## Committed tests\n47|\n48|- Ported reviewer tests kept in `internal/sessquery/rev5_regression_test.go`.\n49|- Added `TestRev5AncestorCheckpointBinding` (wrong-session, wrong-lease,\n50|  wrong-creator ancestor checkpoints, each through BuildPlan,\n51|  Revalidate, AuthoritativeStatus, AuthoritativeList) with shared\n52|  `rev5AncestorFixture` 3-generation control.\n53|- Post-fix: `go test ./internal/sessquery -run '^TestRev5'` — all pass.\n54|\n55|## Narrowing mutants (focused battery, same instrument as committed `testdata/mutate.py`)\n56|\n57|Driver + raw logs + manifest: worktree\n58|`.temp/TASK-260830-21gygk/mutants-rev5/` (ignored scratch;\n59|`mutants-rev5.json` manifest, per-plant `.log` files with real exits).\n60|Each plant keeps the gate and admits exactly one member; files restored\n61|with digest verification; controls green.\n62|\n63|| Mutant | Classification | Killed by |\n64|| --- | --- | --- |\n65|| N-ancestor-checkpoint (skip leaseB ancestor) | KILLED (exit 1) | TestRev5AncestorCheckpointAuthority(/missing...), TestRev5AncestorCheckpointBinding(/wrong_session/wrong_lease/wrong_creator) |\n66|| N-checkpoint-holder (admit hostB creator, winner path) | KILLED (exit 1) | TestRev5CheckpointCreatorMustBeHolder(/non_holder) |\n67|| N-ancestor-holder (admit hostB creator, ancestor path) | KILLED (exit 1) | TestRev5AncestorCheckpointBinding(/wrong_creator) |\n68|| C-harmless-comment | SURVIVED (exit 0, applied log) | control — behavior-preserving |\n69|| control-before / control-after | CONTROL exit 0 | — |\n70|\n71|The two holder plants kill disjoint test sets, proving the two guard\n72|sites are distinct and both required. The same three plants were added\n73|to the committed `internal/sessquery/testdata/mutate.py` battery; every\n74|lease.go anchor in the full battery counts exactly 1 occurrence in the\n75|final source (N-chain-self, N-checkpoint-placeholder, N-lease-missing,\n76|C-harmless-comment, plus the 3 new).\n77|\n78|## Validation (all observed this run)\n79|\n80|- `go build ./...` — exit 0.\n81|- `go vet ./internal/sessquery/ ./internal/sessrepo/ ./internal/provhost/` — exit 0.\n82|- `gofmt -l internal/` — clean, no files listed. NOTE correcting the\n83|  prior evidence description: the old `validation-final.log` gofmt\n84|  failure was exit 2 because it passed a nonexistent `cmd/` directory;\n85|  the valid command is `gofmt -l internal/` (no `cmd/` exists in repo).\n86|- `git diff --check -- internal/ README.md` — exit 0.\n87|- `go test ./... -count=1` — all packages ok (sessquery, sessrepo,\n88|  sessstate, provhost, canonicaljson, specdoc, traceability, etc.).\n89|- Coverage: sessquery 87.9%, sessrepo 87.2% of statements.\n90|- No durable writes on these paths (read-only selector leaf); no\n91|  crash/idempotency protocol change — retained creation-crash\n92|  composition tests still green.\n93|\n94|## Docs / traceability\n95|\n96|- `README.md` and `internal/sessquery/TRACEABILITY.md`\n97|  (\"fully validated succession\") now state whole-ancestry plus holder\n98|  binding; TRACEABILITY row 45 names the new tests and mutants.\n99|- `LOGBOOK.md` carries the rev6 rework entry.\n100|\n101|## AC coverage: 8 of 8 rows driven through shared production entries\n102|\n103|Reader.Resolve (UUID/name: TestResolvePinnedPrecedence,\n104|TestResolveBareIdentityUnion; qualified: TestResolveQualifiedSourcesSelectOneIndex,\n105|TestResolveQualifiedSourceNeverFallsBack, TestResolveExplicitSourceReadFailures;\n106|ambiguity: TestResolveExactNamesAndASCIICollisions; sorting:\n107|TestListStatusDerivedFactsAndStableOrder, TestResolvePeerOrderAndReplicatedIdentity),\n108|Reader.BuildPlan/Revalidate/ParsePlan (TestBuildPlanBindsCurrentFacts,\n109|TestRevalidateDetectsEachFactChange, TestValidSuccessorBuildsAndRevalidates,\n110|TestRevalidateUnionParkedCopyRefuses + rev5 ancestry/holder suites),\n111|Reader.AuthoritativeStatus/List (TestAuthoritativeStatusHealthy,\n112|TestAuthoritativeMissingProcessRefusesStatus,\n113|TestAuthoritativeHostNameBound64, TestAuthoritativeAdmitsFullCapabilityRegistry\n114|+ rev5 suites through both entries). Public CLI execution remains the\n115|stated caller-integration bound (0 CLI rows in this leaf).\n116|\n117|## Candidate paths (uncommitted, Story worktree)\n118|\n119|- `internal/sessquery/lease.go` (fix)\n120|- `internal/sessquery/rev5_regression_test.go` (ported + new tests)\n121|- `internal/sessquery/testdata/mutate.py` (3 narrowing plants)\n122|- `internal/sessquery/TRACEABILITY.md`, `README.md`, `LOGBOOK.md` (docs)\n123|- Retained prior CR5 scope untouched (sessrepo checkpoint/lease owners,\n124|  provhost/sessrepo test updates).\n125|- No stray `--help`/mutation-source tree in the candidate diff;\n126|  mutant scratch lives under ignored `.temp/` only.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
