{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c679","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a08917-49c2-7bc0-a7b5-22c36c1af078"},"sequence":407,"recorded_at":1780531400000809,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"727d1962-de67-4017-b172-583d47fe4c9d","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"727d1962-de67-4017-b172-583d47fe4c9d","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"727d1962-de67-4017-b172-583d47fe4c9d"},"call_id":"call_01a089181b6b74f39daee0f550531b48","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-3tq4ns/worktree/internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md`.\n(1979 line(s) above)\n1980|A host being offline does not make a replica owner; only a takeover or fork\n1981|does.\n1982|\n1983|### 5.4 Checkpoint Record\n1984|\n1985|The Checkpoint Record schema is <code>urn:ax:schema:checkpoint</code> version\n1986|<code>1.0.0</code>. Its top-level object is closed and contains exactly:\n1987|\n1988|| Field | Type | Constraint |\n1989|| --- | --- | --- |\n1990|| <code>schema</code> | string | Exact Checkpoint schema identifier |\n1991|| <code>schema_version</code> | semver | Exact <code>1.0.0</code> |\n1992|| <code>checkpoint_id</code> | digest | Canonical object digest |\n1993|| <code>subject_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Equal to <code>session_id</code> |\n1994|| <code>session_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Existing Session Record |\n1995|| <code>lease_epoch</code> | uint53 | Greater than zero and equal to the referenced winning lease |\n1996|| <code>lease_id</code> | UUIDv4 | Equal to that lease's fencing token |\n1997|| <code>safe_boundary</code> | Safe Boundary Evidence | Closed shape below |\n1998|| <code>event_heads</code> | sorted unique digest[1..64] | Authoritative event DAG heads immediately before this object |\n1999|| <code>workspace_manifest_id</code> | digest | Workspace-group Transfer Manifest root |\n2000|| <code>provider_manifest_id</code> | digest or null | Direct native-store/provider snapshot only |\n2001|| <code>task_board_bundle_id</code> | digest or null | Task-board path only |\n2002|| <code>created_by_host_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Current lease holder |\n2003|| <code>created_at</code> | timestamp | Diagnostic only |\n2004|| <code>status</code> | enum | Literal <code>validated</code> |\n2005|| <code>extensions</code> | object | Reverse-DNS extension keys only |\n2006|\n2007|Safe Boundary Evidence is a closed object containing exactly\n2008|<code>provider_id:provider-id</code>,\n2009|<code>provider_version:string[1..128]</code>,\n2010|<code>evidence:provider_api|provider_event|managed_pty|task_board_bridge|accepted_test</code>,\n2011|<code>input_blocked:boolean</code>, <code>foreground_idle:boolean</code>,\n2012|<code>background_idle:boolean</code>, <code>open_processes:uint53</code>, and\n2013|<code>open_database_handles:uint53</code>. A published checkpoint requires all\n2014|three booleans true and both counters zero. Provider-specific scheduled or\n2015|child work is included in <code>background_idle</code> and\n2016|<code>open_processes</code>; an adapter that cannot prove it MUST NOT publish a\n2017|new checkpoint.\n2018|\n2019|The referenced Session Record selects the persistence variant. For\n2020|<code>kind = direct</code>, <code>provider_manifest_id</code> MUST be non-null\n2021|and <code>task_board_bundle_id</code> MUST be null. A backend-resolved provider\n2022|with no portable bytes still uses a provider Transfer Manifest containing its\n2023|validated identity and zero file entries; null is not used to erase that\n2024|distinction. For <code>kind = task_board</code>,\n2025|<code>provider_manifest_id</code> MUST be null and\n2026|<code>task_board_bundle_id</code> MUST be non-null. Both-null and both-non-null\n2027|checkpoints are invalid.\n2028|\n2029|A checkpoint MUST NOT be published until every referenced object exists,\n2030|hashes correctly, passes schema validation, and the provider/task-board path\n2031|meets its quiescence requirement. A force takeover MAY select the newest\n2032|validated checkpoint even when no new safe checkpoint can be created.\n2033|\n2034|<code>event_heads</code> identifies the authoritative event DAG immediately\n2035|before the checkpoint object. A later <code>checkpoint.created</code> event MAY\n2036|reference that checkpoint and those heads; the checkpoint MUST NOT reference\n2037|the announcing event because that would create a circular digest dependency.\n2038|The transitive event-head closure also fixes the Section 2.4 effective\n2039|execution profile and its nullable source event for this checkpoint. A missing,\n2040|losing-lease, or non-newest <code>profile.changed</code> reference is\n2041|<code>integrity_failure</code>; checkpoint consumers MUST NOT consult a later\n2042|local-only profile event or fall back to the creation profile.\n2043|\n2044|Normative negative fixtures are: <code>CP-N1</code>, with\n2045|<code>background_idle = false</code> and status <code>validated</code>;\n2046|<code>CP-N2</code>, with a direct Session Record and null provider manifest;\n2047|<code>CP-N3</code>, with both persistence IDs non-null; and\n2048|<code>CP-N4</code>, with an unknown <code>safe_boundary.pid</code> member. Each\n2049|MUST be rejected with <code>incompatible_schema</code> before publication.\n2050|\n2051|Normative example:\n2052|\n2053|~~~json\n2054|{\n2055|  \"schema\": \"urn:ax:schema:checkpoint\",\n2056|  \"schema_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n2057|  \"checkpoint_id\": \"sha256:e051996f51f13ace4f5cdebe1e30fd26fd5fe104cfd6e6a7f9f1206ba3819656\",\n2058|  \"subject_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n2059|  \"session_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c67b","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a08917-49c2-7bc0-a7b5-22c36c1af078"},"sequence":408,"recorded_at":1780531400000811,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"727d1962-de67-4017-b172-583d47fe4c9d","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"727d1962-de67-4017-b172-583d47fe4c9d","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"727d1962-de67-4017-b172-583d47fe4c9d"},"call_id":"call_01a089181c967ce19373b6aea1d0096c","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-3tq4ns/worktree/internal/sessquery/query.go`.\n1|// Package sessquery is the single shared selector API over the session\n2|// repository and state projector: read-only selector resolution\n3|// (Section 14.7.1 literal grammar over Section 2.3 tiers), local\n4|// list/status summaries, and immutable SelectionPlan construction with\n5|// current-fact revalidation (Section 14.7.2). CLI and lifecycle callers\n6|// own invoking this API at every required boundary; no second resolver\n7|// exists. Unknown owner/lease facts and parked diagnostics stay explicit\n8|// in Projection: host display names, checkpoint timestamps/age,\n9|// workspace state, capabilities, process liveness and sync timestamps\n10|// require their respective observation owners and are never inferred\n11|// from a record or a successful read.\n12|package sessquery\n13|\n14|import (\n15|\t\"errors\"\n16|\t\"fmt\"\n17|\t\"sort\"\n18|\t\"strings\"\n19|\n20|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/scalar\"\n21|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/sessrepo\"\n22|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/sessstate\"\n23|)\n24|\n25|var (\n26|\tErrUnavailable = errors.New(\"session index unavailable\")\n27|\tErrAmbiguous   = sessrepo.ErrNameAmbiguous\n28|\tErrNotFound    = sessrepo.ErrNameNotFound\n29|\t// ErrInvalidArgument refuses a malformed caller argument: selector\n30|\t// grammar violations (empty key, unknown source prefix, malformed\n31|\t// durable IDs, overlong argument), malformed plan members, unknown\n32|\t// action tags, and malformed destinations or expectations. Wire\n33|\t// exit binding for a CLI surface belongs to that surface's leaf;\n34|\t// this library keeps the refusal class distinct and stable.\n35|\tErrInvalidArgument = errors.New(\"invalid_arguments\")\n36|\t// ErrSourceNotFound reports that complete valid configuration has\n37|\t// no requested explicit source.\n38|\tErrSourceNotFound = errors.New(\"selector_source_not_found\")\n39|\t// ErrPeerNotAllowlisted reports an explicitly selected peer that\n40|\t// is configured but not allowlisted, including authorization\n41|\t// revoked after a plan was built.\n42|\tErrPeerNotAllowlisted = errors.New(\"peer_not_allowlisted\")\n43|\t// ErrSourceReadFailed reports a remote source transport/I-O read\n44|\t// failure with no fallback. The underlying cause stays attached\n45|\t// for errors.Is, so a repository-path failure remains visible as\n46|\t// such. A local source/store I-O failure keeps its repository\n47|\t// error, which the CLI Result 5 leaf maps to\n48|\t// local_precondition_failed; a partial or malformed index or\n49|\t// authority response is integrity failure, not absence.\n50|\tErrSourceReadFailed = errors.New(\"selector_source_read_failed\")\n51|\t// ErrInvalidConfig reports duplicate or malformed effective source\n52|\t// mappings: duplicate exact aliases or host IDs, a peer host that\n53|\t// collides with the local host, malformed host IDs, or aliases\n54|\t// outside the configured 1-64 printable-character bound.\n55|\tErrInvalidConfig = errors.New(\"invalid_config\")\n56|\t// ErrPlanStale reports bound selection facts that changed after a\n57|\t// plan was built; a fresh plan and confirmation are required. The\n58|\t// wrapped reason names the first diverged member in compare order.\n59|\tErrPlanStale = errors.New(\"selector_plan_stale\")\n60|\t// ErrBootstrapIncomplete reports a complete authority read proving\n61|\t// a Session Record without any valid lease: an interrupted\n62|\t// persistence prefix for the bootstrap-recovery leaf (Section\n63|\t// 14.7.4), never a public summary. A failed read keeps its\n64|\t// read-failure class instead; corrupt authority is integrity\n65|\t// failure. Wire exit binding for a CLI surface belongs to that\n66|\t// surface's leaf; this library keeps the refusal class distinct\n67|\t// and stable.\n68|\tErrBootstrapIncomplete = errors.New(\"selector_bootstrap_incomplete\")\n69|\t// ErrObservationUnavailable reports a required summary observation\n70|\t// or host metadata fact that cannot be established from validated\n71|\t// inputs. Nothing is inferred in its place: no source alias stands\n72|\t// in for host metadata, and no absent observation mints liveness,\n73|\t// capability, workspace, or timestamp facts.\n74|\tErrObservationUnavailable = errors.New(\"selector_observation_unavailable\")\n75|)\n76|\n77|// PeerIndex binds a peer identity to its already persisted learned index.\n78|// Transport/authentication and installing peer indexes are upstream owners;\n79|// this reader does not fetch, authenticate, or attest a caller-supplied index.\n80|type PeerIndex struct {\n81|\tHostID string\n82|\tRepo   *sessrepo.Repository\n83|}\n84|\n85|// Reader reads existing indexes. AllowlistedPeerIDs must come from the owning\n86|// configuration layer, separately from the learned indexes. An unlisted source\n87|// is never read. Failed reads from listed sources are errors, never\n88|// empty indexes that let resolution fall through to a lower-priority UUID.\n89|// LocalHostID comes from the local host identity owner; empty preserves unknown.\n90|//\n91|// Aliases carries the exact configured peer-alias mapping (host ID to\n92|// alias) from the same configuration owner, kept separate from the\n93|// learned index handles: a mapping without a handle contributes no\n94|// learned names, and a handle without a mapping stays reachable through\n95|// the bare union and the \"id:\" host form but never through \"peer:\".\n96|// Alias comparison is always exact, never folded, trimmed, or decoded.\n97|//\n98|// HostMetadata and Observations carry the validated host and observation\n99|// facts the authoritative summary layer requires, from their respective\n100|// owners. They are consulted only by that layer: List and Status keep\n101|// the internal read model and refuse only the unrepresentable\n102|// record-only bootstrap.\n103|//\n104|// LeaseRecords carries the validated winning-lease authority for plan\n105|// construction and revalidation, from the lease owner. Each entry is\n106|// canonical JSON for one urn:ax:schema:lease Lease Record; the reader\n107|// validates the closed shape and canonical self identity through the\n108|// canonicaljson owner, selects the greatest (epoch, lease_id) winner\n109|// per session, and binds that record digest with its tuple and holder.\n110|// Absence for a session refuses observation_unavailable; malformed\n111|// bytes refuse invalid_config. Envelope observations never substitute\n112|// for these records.\n113|//\n114|// CheckpointRecords carries the validated checkpoint authority the\n115|// winning-lease succession gate requires, from the checkpoint owner.\n116|// Each entry is canonical JSON for one urn:ax:schema:checkpoint\n117|// Checkpoint Record; the reader validates the closed shape and\n118|// canonical self identity through the sessrepo owner. Every successor\n119|// winner must reference an admitted record for its session and\n120|// predecessor lease; an unresolvable reference refuses\n121|// observation_unavailable, and malformed bytes refuse invalid_config.\n122|type Reader struct {\n123|\tLocal              *sessrepo.Repository\n124|\tLocalHostID        string\n125|\tAllowlistedPeerIDs []string\n126|\tPeers              []PeerIndex\n127|\tAliases            map[string]string\n128|\tHostMetadata       map[string]HostMetadata\n129|\tObservations       map[string]SessionObservations\n130|\tLeaseRecords       [][]byte\n131|\tCheckpointRecords  [][]byte\n132|}\n133|\n134|// Summary contains only facts derived from verified session records and events.\n135|// It is an internal read model, not the closed Section 14.2 CLI SessionSummary.\n136|// Unknown owner/lease and parked diagnostics remain explicit in Projection.\n137|// Host display names, checkpoint timestamps/age, workspace state, capabilities,\n138|// process liveness and sync timestamps require their respective observation\n139|// owners and are deliberately not inferred from a record or a successful read.\n140|type Summary struct {\n141|\tProjection sessstate.Projection\n142|}\n143|\n144|// List reads local summaries in bytewise session-ID order. Parked sessions stay\n145|// visible with their blocking reason and retry; failure to enumerate the index\n146|// fails the read. No durable state is written, even for an interrupted create.\n147|// A complete read proving a record without any valid lease refuses the whole\n148|// list with selector_bootstrap_incomplete: the interrupted prefix is never\n149|// silently omitted and never returned as a public summary.\n150|func (reader *Reader) List() ([]Summary, error) {\n151|\tif reader == nil || reader.Local == nil {\n152|\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"%w: local repository is required\", ErrUnavailable)\n153|\t}\n154|\trows, err := reader.read(reader.Local)\n155|\tif err != nil {\n156|\t\treturn nil, err\n157|\t}\n158|\tfor _, row := range rows {\n159|\t\tif err := checkSummaryRepresentable(row); err != nil {\n160|\t\t\treturn nil, err\n161|\t\t}\n162|\t}\n163|\treturn rows, nil\n164|}\n165|\n166|func (reader *Reader) read(repo *sessrepo.Repository) ([]Summary, error) {\n167|\trows, err := repo.ListSessions()\n168|\tif err != nil {\n169|\t\treturn nil, err\n170|\t}\n171|\tout := make([]Summary, 0, len(rows))\n172|\tprojector := sessstate.Projector{Repo: repo, LocalHostID: reader.LocalHostID}\n173|\tfor _, row := range rows {\n174|\t\tprojection, err := projector.Project(row.SessionID)\n175|\t\tif err != nil {\n176|\t\t\treturn nil, err\n177|\t\t}\n178|\t\tout = append(out, Summary{Projection: projection})\n179|\t}\n180|\tsort.Slice(out, func(i, j int) bool { return out[i].Projection.SessionID < out[j].Projection.SessionID })\n181|\treturn out, nil\n182|}\n183|\n184|// Status resolves any selector — bare, \"id:\", or source-qualified — through\n185|// the same path as Resolve, then projects from the selected repository. It\n186|// never treats a failed read as not found. Parked sessions can be inspected\n187|// by ID through InspectLocal, independently of live-name routing, so\n188|// operators retain access to the recovery diagnostics.\n189|func (reader *Reader) Status(selector string) (Summary, error) {\n190|\tselected, err := reader.Resolve(selector)\n191|\tif err != nil {\n192|\t\treturn Summary{}, err\n193|\t}\n194|\tprojection, err := (&sessstate.Projector{Repo: selected.repo, LocalHostID: reader.LocalHostID}).Project(selected.SessionID)\n195|\tif err != nil {\n196|\t\treturn Summary{}, err\n197|\t}\n198|\tsummary := Summary{Projection: projection}\n199|\tif err := checkSummaryRepresentable(summary); err != nil {\n200|\t\treturn Summary{}, err\n201|\t}\n202|\treturn summary, nil\n203|}\n204|\n205|// InspectLocal reads one local ID, including a parked or tombstoned session.\n206|func (reader *Reader) InspectLocal(sessionID string) (Summary, error) {\n207|\tif reader == nil || reader.Local == nil {\n208|\t\treturn Summary{}, fmt.Errorf(\"%w: local repository is required\", ErrUnavailable)\n209|\t}\n210|\tprojection, err := (&sessstate.Projector{Repo: reader.Local, LocalHostID: reader.LocalHostID}).Project(sessionID)\n211|\tif err != nil {\n212|\t\treturn Summary{}, err\n213|\t}\n214|\treturn Summary{Projection: projection}, nil\n215|}\n216|\n217|// Selection identifies the session and source index, never an attach or mutation\n218|// plan. PeerHostID is empty for local resolution; it is not the winning owner.\n219|type Selection struct {\n220|\tSessionID  string\n221|\tPeerHostID string\n222|\trepo       *sessrepo.Repository\n223|}\n224|\n225|type candidate struct {\n226|\tsummary   Summary\n227|\tselection Selection\n228|}\n229|\n230|// Resolve applies one parsed selector through the single shared path:\n231|// grammar first, then effective-configuration validation, then the\n232|// source tier. A bare selector retains the exact Section 2.3 tiers:\n233|// local exact live name, allowlisted peer exact live name, exact UUID,\n234|// not found. An \"id:\" key bypasses names for the durable UUID in the\n235|// local and allowed-peer union. A qualified selector resolves its key\n236|// in exactly one source index with no fallback. ASCII folding detects\n237|// collisions within each name tier; it does not turn a unique case\n238|// variant into an exact match. Repository-parked entries (failed reads,\n239|// never tombstone evidence) and tombstoned entries (authoritative\n240|// tombstone evidence) are not live candidates. A tier that must be\n241|// read but cannot be read is a read failure, not permission to proceed\n242|// to a lower tier. This is logical index eligibility, not proof of\n243|// process liveness or safe attach/resume readiness; those decisions\n244|// belong to the action planner invoking plans at its boundaries.\n245|func (reader *Reader) Resolve(selector string) (Selection, error) {\n246|\tparsed, err := ParseSelector(selector)\n247|\tif err != nil {\n248|\t\treturn Selection{}, err\n249|\t}\n250|\tif reader == nil || reader.Local == nil {\n251|\t\treturn Selection{}, fmt.Errorf(\"%w: local repository is required\", ErrUnavailable)\n252|\t}\n253|\tconfig, err := reader.validatedConfiguration()\n254|\tif err != nil {\n255|\t\treturn Selection{}, err\n256|\t}\n257|\tif parsed.Source != SourceBare {\n258|\t\treturn reader.resolveExplicit(parsed, config)\n259|\t}\n260|\treturn reader.resolveBare(parsed, config)\n261|}\n262|\n263|// resolveBare applies the Section 2.3 tiers over the local and\n264|// allowed-peer union. Unread lower tiers are never consulted after a\n265|// unique higher-tier match; a tier that must be read but cannot be\n266|// read fails the resolution instead of falling through.\n267|func (reader *Reader) resolveBare(parsed Selector, config validatedConfig) (Selection, error) {\n268|\tlocal, err := reader.read(reader.Local)\n269|\tif err != nil {\n270|\t\treturn Selection{}, err\n271|\t}\n272|\tlocalLive := liveCandidates(local, reader.Local, \"\")\n273|\t// Peer tiers read lazily: a unique local name match never depends\n274|\t// on lower-tier reads, but any tier that must be read and cannot\n275|\t// be read fails instead of falling through.\n276|\tpeers, peersRead := []candidate(nil), false\n277|\treadPeers := func() ([]candidate, error) {\n278|\t\tif !peersRead {\n279|\t\t\tpeersRead = true\n280|\t\t\tvar err error\n281|\t\t\tpeers, err = reader.peerCandidates()\n282|\t\t\tif err != nil {\n283|\t\t\t\treturn nil, err\n284|\t\t\t}\n285|\t\t}\n286|\t\treturn peers, nil\n287|\t}\n288|\tif parsed.IDKey {\n289|\t\tunion, err := readPeers()\n290|\t\tif err != nil {\n291|\t\t\treturn Selection{}, err\n292|\t\t}\n293|\t\treturn selectIdentity(strings.TrimPrefix(parsed.Key, \"id:\"), append(localLive, union...), config)\n294|\t}\n295|\tif match, found, err := matchName(localLive, parsed.Key); found || err != nil {\n296|\t\treturn match, err\n297|\t}\n298|\tunion, err := readPeers()\n299|\tif err != nil {\n300|\t\treturn Selection{}, err\n301|\t}\n302|\tif match, found, err := matchName(union, parsed.Key); found || err != nil {\n303|\t\tif err != nil {\n304|\t\t\treturn Selection{}, err\n305|\t\t}\n306|\t\tif err := checkRecordAgreement(append(append([]candidate(nil), localLive...), union...), match); err != nil {\n307|\t\t\treturn Selection{}, err\n308|\t\t}\n309|\t\treturn match, nil\n310|\t}\n311|\tif parsed.UUIDShaped {\n312|\t\treturn selectIdentity(parsed.Key, append(localLive, union...), config)\n313|\t}\n314|\treturn Selection{}, fmt.Errorf(\"%w: no live session named %q\", ErrNotFound, parsed.Raw)\n315|}\n316|\n317|func liveCandidates(rows []Summary, repo *sessrepo.Repository, peer string) []candidate {\n318|\tout := make([]candidate, 0, len(rows))\n319|\tfor _, row := range rows {\n320|\t\tif row.Projection.Parked != nil || row.Projection.State == sessstate.StateTombstoned {\n321|\t\t\tcontinue\n322|\t\t}\n323|\t\tout = append(out, candidate{row, Selection{row.Projection.SessionID, peer, repo}})\n324|\t}\n325|\treturn out\n326|}\n327|\n328|// resolveExplicit selects a key in exactly one configured source index.\n329|// An explicit source never falls back to the local index, another peer,\n330|// a cached index from another source, or a union search, even when the\n331|// same name or UUID exists there: a miss in the selected source is not\n332|// found, and a source that cannot be completely read is a read failure.\n333|func (reader *Reader) resolveExplicit(parsed Selector, config validatedConfig) (Selection, error) {\n334|\trepo, peerHost, err := reader.locateSource(parsed, config)\n335|\tif err != nil {\n336|\t\treturn Selection{}, err\n337|\t}\n338|\trows, err := reader.readSource(repo, peerHost)\n339|\tif err != nil {\n340|\t\treturn Selection{}, err\n341|\t}\n342|\tlive := liveCandidates(rows, repo, peerHost)\n343|\tif parsed.IDKey {\n344|\t\treturn selectIdentity(strings.TrimPrefix(parsed.Key, \"id:\"), live, config)\n345|\t}\n346|\tif match, found, err := matchName(live, parsed.Key); found || err != nil {\n347|\t\treturn match, err\n348|\t}\n349|\tif parsed.UUIDShaped {\n350|\t\treturn selectIdentity(parsed.Key, live, config)\n351|\t}\n352|\treturn Selection{}, fmt.Errorf(\"%w: no live session named %q in source %s\", ErrNotFound, parsed.Key, describeSource(parsed))\n353|}\n354|\n355|// locateSource maps an explicit source to its index handle. An explicit\n356|// unknown alias or host is selector_source_not_found; a known but\n357|// disallowed peer is peer_not_allowlisted. The local source is always\n358|// admitted and needs no allowlist entry.\n359|func (reader *Reader) locateSource(parsed Selector, config validatedConfig) (*sessrepo.Repository, string, error) {\n360|\tswitch parsed.Source {\n361|\tcase SourceLocal:\n362|\t\treturn reader.Local, \"\", nil\n363|\tcase SourcePeerAlias:\n364|\t\thost, ok := config.hostForAlias(reader, parsed.SourceValue)\n365|\t\tif !ok {\n366|\t\t\treturn nil, \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"%w: no configured source for alias %q\", ErrSourceNotFound, parsed.SourceValue)\n367|\t\t}\n368|\t\tif _, allowed := config.allowed[host]; !allowed {\n369|\t\t\treturn nil, \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"%w: peer %s is not allowlisted\", ErrPeerNotAllowlisted, host)\n370|\t\t}\n371|\t\treturn reader.peerRepo(host)\n372|\tcase SourcePeerHost:\n373|\t\tif config.localHost != \"\" && parsed.SourceValue == config.localHost {\n374|\t\t\treturn reader.Local, \"\", nil\n375|\t\t}\n376|\t\tif !knownPeer(reader, parsed.SourceValue) {\n377|\t\t\treturn nil, \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"%w: no configured source for host %s\", ErrSourceNotFound, parsed.SourceValue)\n378|\t\t}\n379|\t\tif _, allowed := config.allowed[parsed.SourceValue]; !allowed {\n380|\t\t\treturn nil, \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"%w: peer %s is not allowlisted\", ErrPeerNotAllowlisted, parsed.SourceValue)\n381|\t\t}\n382|\t\treturn reader.peerRepo(parsed.SourceValue)\n383|\tdefault:\n384|\t\treturn nil, \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"%w: unknown selector source\", ErrInvalidArgument)\n385|\t}\n386|}\n387|\n388|// knownPeer reports whether a host carries a configured learned index,\n389|// regardless of allowlisting or readability.\n390|func knownPeer(reader *Reader, host string) bool {\n391|\tfor _, peer := range reader.Peers {\n392|\t\tif peer.HostID == host {\n393|\t\t\treturn true\n394|\t\t}\n395|\t}\n396|\treturn false\n397|}\n398|\n399|// peerRepo binds one allowlisted peer host to its learned index handle.\n400|// A peer with no advertised index cannot be completely read, so\n401|// explicit selection refuses with the read-failure class instead of\n402|// treating the source as absent; union tiers simply learn nothing from\n403|// it. A listed index with an unavailable repository is the same failed\n404|// observation.\n405|func (reader *Reader) peerRepo(host string) (*sessrepo.Repository, string, error) {\n406|\tseen := false\n407|\tvar repo *sessrepo.Repository\n408|\tfor _, peer := range reader.Peers {\n409|\t\tif peer.HostID != host {\n410|\t\t\tcontinue\n411|\t\t}\n412|\t\tif seen {\n413|\t\t\treturn nil, \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"%w: multiple indexes for peer %s\", ErrUnavailable, host)\n414|\t\t}\n415|\t\tseen = true\n416|\t\trepo = peer.Repo\n417|\t}\n418|\tif !seen {\n419|\t\treturn nil, \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"%w: peer %s advertises no learned index\", ErrSourceReadFailed, host)\n420|\t}\n421|\tif repo == nil {\n422|\t\treturn nil, \"\", peerReadFailed(host, fmt.Errorf(\"%w: unreadable index for peer %s\", ErrUnavailable, host))\n423|\t}\n424|\treturn repo, host, nil\n425|}\n426|\n427|// readSource completes one source read. Local I-O failures keep their\n428|// repository error; remote failures carry the read-failure class while\n429|// preserving the underlying cause for errors.Is.\n430|func (reader *Reader) readSource(repo *sessrepo.Repository, peerHost string) ([]Summary, error) {\n431|\trows, err := reader.read(repo)\n432|\tif err != nil {\n433|\t\tif peerHost == \"\" {\n434|\t\t\treturn nil, err\n435|\t\t}\n436|\t\treturn nil, peerReadFailed(peerHost, err)\n437|\t}\n438|\treturn rows, nil\n439|}\n440|\n441|// peerReadFailed marks a remote-source read failure with its contract\n442|// class while preserving the underlying cause: a failed read is never\n443|// an absence that lets resolution fall through to another source.\n444|func peerReadFailed(host string, err error) error {\n445|\treturn errors.Join(fmt.Errorf(\"%w: peer %s index read failed\", ErrSourceReadFailed, host), err)\n446|}\n447|\n448|// describeSource names the selected source for refusal evidence: exact\n449|// literal alias or host, never a display name.\n450|func describeSource(parsed Selector) string {\n451|\tswitch parsed.Source {\n452|\tcase SourceLocal:\n453|\t\treturn \"local\"\n454|\tcase SourcePeerAlias:\n455|\t\treturn fmt.Sprintf(\"peer:%s\", parsed.SourceValue)\n456|\tcase SourcePeerHost:\n457|\t\treturn fmt.Sprintf(\"id:%s\", parsed.SourceValue)\n458|\tdefault:\n459|\t\treturn \"bare\"\n460|\t}\n461|}\n462|\n463|// selectIdentity selects a durable session UUID from live candidates\n464|// independent of names: the \"id:\" key form and the UUID tier. Copies\n465|// of one UUID deduplicate only when their immutable record digests\n466|// agree; disagreeing copies are inconsistent authority\n467|// (integrity_failure), not an ambiguity. Identical copies select the\n468|// bytewise smallest holder host.\n469|func selectIdentity(uuid string, pool []candidate, config validatedConfig) (Selection, error) {\n470|\tid, err := scalar.ParseUUIDv7(uuid)\n471|\tif err != nil {\n472|\t\treturn Selection{}, fmt.Errorf(\"%w: malformed session UUID: %v\", ErrInvalidArgument, err)\n473|\t}\n474|\tvar matches []candidate\n475|\tfor _, item := range pool {\n476|\t\tif item.selection.SessionID == id.String() {\n477|\t\t\tmatches = append(matches, item)\n478|\t\t}\n479|\t}\n480|\tif len(matches) == 0 {\n481|\t\treturn Selection{}, fmt.Errorf(\"%w: no live session with ID %q\", ErrNotFound, id.String())\n482|\t}\n483|\tfor _, item := range matches[1:] {\n484|\t\tif item.summary.Projection.RecordID != matches[0].summary.Projection.RecordID {\n485|\t\t\treturn Selection{}, fmt.Errorf(\"%w: session %s carries disagreeing record digests across sources\", sessstate.ErrIntegrity, id.String())\n486|\t\t}\n487|\t}\n488|\tbest := matches[0]\n489|\tfor _, item := range matches[1:] {\n490|\t\tif holderHost(item.selection.PeerHostID, config.localHost) < holderHost(best.selection.PeerHostID, config.localHost) {\n491|\t\t\tbest = item\n492|\t\t}\n493|\t}\n494|\treturn best.selection, nil\n495|}\n496|\n497|// holderHost orders copy holders bytewise for the deterministic tie\n498|// break. PeerHostID is empty for local copies; while the local host\n499|// identity is unknown the local copy sorts before every peer,\n500|// preserving local priority there.\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
