{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c6ad","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a08917-49c2-7bc0-a7b5-22c36c1af078"},"sequence":433,"recorded_at":1780531400000861,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"727d1962-de67-4017-b172-583d47fe4c9d","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"727d1962-de67-4017-b172-583d47fe4c9d","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"727d1962-de67-4017-b172-583d47fe4c9d"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a08918-27e1-7f40-aa5e-81520254647a"},"task_id":"01a08918-27e1-7f40-aa5e-81520254647a","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a08918-27e1-7f40-aa5e-81520254647a","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-3tq4ns/worktree/internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md`.\n(1449 line(s) above)\n1450|The background service integration is:\n1451|\n1452|- a launchd agent on macOS;\n1453|- a systemd user unit on Linux and WSL2 where systemd is enabled;\n1454|- otherwise an explicitly installed per-user periodic launcher on WSL2; and\n1455|- a Scheduled Task or per-user service on native Windows.\n1456|\n1457|The service MAY run periodic sync, peer health checks, tombstone\n1458|acknowledgement, stale-process detection, and wrapper restoration. Core commands\n1459|MUST work without it. Service absence MUST degrade freshness, not corrupt\n1460|ownership.\n1461|\n1462|The macOS launchd background control plane and Aqua terminal broker are separate\n1463|roles. The control plane MUST NOT acquire GUI/Keychain authority by proxy and\n1464|MUST NOT create a credential-dependent tmux server. The Aqua broker exposes\n1465|only authenticated, same-user, generation-bound terminal readiness and server\n1466|operations; it does not gain lease, workspace, provider, or replication\n1467|authority.\n1468|\n1469|## 5. Domain records and state machine\n1470|\n1471|### 5.1 Session Record\n1472|\n1473|This subsection defines the immutable Session Record <code>1.0.0</code> base\n1474|variant. It is created exactly once and uses schema\n1475|<code>urn:ax:schema:session-record</code> version <code>1.0.0</code>. Sections\n1476|5.1.1 and 5.1.2 define the independently closed <code>2.0.0</code> and\n1477|<code>3.0.0</code> variants used by clone and unified-derivation writers; they do\n1478|not mutate or widen the base variant.\n1479|\n1480|| Field | Type | Constraint |\n1481|| --- | --- | --- |\n1482|| <code>schema</code> | string | Exact schema identifier |\n1483|| <code>schema_version</code> | semver | <code>1.0.0</code> |\n1484|| <code>record_id</code> | digest | Canonical object digest |\n1485|| <code>subject_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Equal to <code>session_id</code> |\n1486|| <code>session_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Globally unique |\n1487|| <code>name</code> | string | Section 2.3 grammar |\n1488|| <code>kind</code> | enum | <code>direct</code> or <code>task_board</code> |\n1489|| <code>created_at</code> | timestamp | Diagnostic time |\n1490|| <code>created_by_host_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Allowlisted host at creation |\n1491|| <code>provider_id</code> | string | Lowercase plugin ID |\n1492|| <code>workspace_group_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Required |\n1493|| <code>execution_profile</code> | enum | <code>standard</code> or <code>yolo</code> |\n1494|| <code>launch_plan</code> | Launch Plan | Closed shape below; sanitized and secret-free |\n1495|| <code>task_board</code> | Task-board Reference or null | Required object exactly when <code>kind = task_board</code> |\n1496|| <code>fork_provenance</code> | Fork Provenance or null | Required object exactly when this record was created by fork |\n1497|| <code>extensions</code> | object | Required; may be empty; reverse-DNS keys only |\n1498|\n1499|The embedded Launch Plan is a closed object with exactly these members:\n1500|\n1501|| Field | Type | Constraint |\n1502|| --- | --- | --- |\n1503|| <code>argv</code> | array&lt;string&gt;[1..128] | Each element is 1–4,096 UTF-8 bytes; total encoded argv is at most 65,536 bytes; never a shell command string |\n1504|| <code>cwd_workspace_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Names one workspace in the Session Record's workspace group |\n1505|| <code>cwd_relative</code> | string | <code>.</code> for the workspace root or a path satisfying Section 1.6 |\n1506|| <code>env_names</code> | array&lt;string&gt;[0..64] | Sorted, unique names matching <code>[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]{0,127}</code>; values resolve only from destination-local state |\n1507|| <code>env_literals</code> | map(environment-name,string)[0..64] | Non-secret literals of at most 4,096 UTF-8 bytes each; keys sorted in canonical form and disjoint from <code>env_names</code> |\n1508|| <code>contains_secrets</code> | boolean | MUST be false |\n1509|| <code>extensions</code> | object | Reverse-DNS extension keys only |\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
