{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d3db","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a08917-49c2-7bc0-a7b5-22c36c1af078"},"sequence":2120,"recorded_at":1780531400004235,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"727d1962-de67-4017-b172-583d47fe4c9d","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"727d1962-de67-4017-b172-583d47fe4c9d","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"727d1962-de67-4017-b172-583d47fe4c9d"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a08922-028e-7a21-99c7-8297a51708fe"},"task_id":"01a08922-028e-7a21-99c7-8297a51708fe","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a08922-028e-7a21-99c7-8297a51708fe","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-50-1\",\n  \"command\": \"task-board m 'get(TASK-260830-21gygk) { progress }' 2>&1 | python3 -c \\\"import sys,json; d=json.load(sys.stdin); print(json.dumps(d, indent=1)[:6000])\\\"\",\n  \"description\": \"Read task checklist state\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"{\\n \\\"blockedBy\\\": [\\n  \\\"TASK-260830-1r9wrr\\\",\\n  \\\"TASK-260908-2tkufa\\\",\\n  \\\"STORY-260908-18woqo\\\"\\n ],\\n \\\"checklist\\\": [\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Production entry points implement the scoped deliverable: Resolve UUID/name/qualified selectors, ambiguity, list/status summaries, and stable deterministic sorting\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": false\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Relevant positive, negative, compatibility, and recovery tests pass with logs attached\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"README/doctor/capability evidence and specification traceability are updated without unsupported claims\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": false\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Code written per task description and AC\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": false\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Relevant tests written for new or changed behavior and passing\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Every command, message, state, or refusal named in the AC is driven through the production entry point by a named committed test, or is declared a stated bound. Report coverage as a ratio \\\\u2014 `n of m AC rows driven` \\\\u2014 and name the production call site for each. Prose in place of the ratio is not evidence.\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Gating, refusing, validating, authorizing, or attesting behavior covered by negative tests that fail when the gate admits what it must reject, with the production call site named\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": false\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Every gate ships at least one NARROWING mutant \\\\u2014 the gate stays present and is weakened to admit exactly one member of the class it must reject, and a named test must fail. A delete-only mutant proves only that the gate exists and is not accepted as evidence.\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": false\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"A gate that inspects source text is additionally attacked by a mutant that PRESERVES the searched-for token and changes behavior, and the mutant harness executes the behavioral suite, not only the static checker.\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Lint clean\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Relevant build/validation commands run after changes and build not broken\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"New outcome artifact attached on the board with a task-scoped name when the work produces notes, logs, screenshots, or other deliverables\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Important findings, decisions, anomalies, or regressions recorded in logbook when relevant\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"In a managed Story worktree the candidate is left UNCOMMITTED in the worktree for the handoff to snapshot \\\\u2014 never commit on the Story branch. A producer commit moves the branch tip off the recorded checkpoint and the handoff refuses with change_request_candidate_committed_past_checkpoint; repair with `git reset --soft <checkpoint_oid>` before completing again.\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Implementation matches AC\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": false\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Solution fits project architecture\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Tests green\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Gate, refusal, validation, authorization, and attestation behavior attacked, not read \\\\u2014 positive-path-only evidence is not accepted\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": false\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"If review does not accept the work \\\\u2014 verdict evidence added and status routed by the explicit verdict branches\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  }\\n ],\\n \\\"derivedBlockedBy\\\": [],\\n \\\"estimate\\\": {\\n  \\\"kind\\\": \\\"estimated\\\",\\n  \\\"scale\\\": {\\n   \\\"kind\\\": \\\"fibonacci\\\",\\n   \\\"number\\\": 5\\n  }\\n },\\n \\\"id\\\": \\\"TASK-260830-21gygk\\\",\\n \\\"integrationCheckpointed\\\": false,\\n \\\"isAdvisoryBlocked\\\": false,\\n \\\"isBlocked\\\": false,\\n \\\"notes\\\": \\\"STORY-260830-3tq4ns base refresh: the Story branch was replayed onto trunk 7654d7cadb2c before this final-leaf producer started; the reviewed trunk OID is 7654d7cadb2c\\\\nspawn run RUN-260907-454092 failed; operator action required; failure: spawn failed before runner ownership transfer\\\\nspawn workload selection: class=implementation source=explicit policy=spawn.workload_classes pair=codex/gpt-6-astra/high pair_source=explicit match=recommended_rank_1 snapshot=sha256:1a9f7ab7a51ebcfe90e2c5d151e77598d3c077049ceeff96b3b445f0585610e0 rationale=\\\\\\\"Complex final-leaf name resolution and deterministic summaries require Astra high with independent review and full validation.\\\\\\\"\\\\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: codex via explicit_override (preferred_agentic_system: exclusive[codex], config: spawn.preferred_agentic_system)\\\\nspawn launch composition: empty; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=codex; schema=1; producer=v1.6.1-128-gab60e0d; diagnostic=launch_composition_empty; no project MCP servers enabled\\\\nspawn queued: [implementer] developer (codex) (run=RUN-260907-c21363, max_parallel=20)\\\\nspawn run started: [implementer] developer (codex) (run=RUN-260907-c21363)\\\\nSTORY-260830-3tq4ns base refresh: the Story branch was replayed onto trunk 7654d7cadb2c before this final-leaf producer started; the reviewed trunk OID is 7654d7cadb2c\\\\nspawn run RUN-260907-454092 failed; operator action required; failure: spawn failed before runner ownership transfer\\\\nspawn workload selection: class=implementation source=explicit policy=spawn.workload_classes pair=codex/gpt-6-astra/high pair_source=explicit match=recommended_rank_1 snapshot=sha256:1a9f7ab7a51ebcfe90e2c5d151e77598d3c077049ceeff96b3b445f0585610e0 rationale=\\\\\\\"Complex final-leaf name resolution and deterministic summaries require Astra high with independent review and full validation.\\\\\\\"\\\\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: codex via explicit_override (preferred_agentic_system: exclusive[codex], config: spawn.preferred_agentic_system)\\\\nspawn launch composition: empty; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=codex; schema=1; producer=v1.6.1-128-gab60e0d; diagnostic=launch_composition_empty; no project MCP servers enabled\\\\nspawn queued: [implementer] developer (codex) (run=RUN-260907-c21363, max_parallel=20)\\\\nspawn run started: [implementer] developer (codex) (run=RUN-260907-c21363)\\\\nRUN-260907-c21363 Stop-The-Line: pinned v0.5.0 \\\\\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 6001,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1501,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
